# gateway/app.d/*.caddy — per-app gateway snippets.
#
# This directory is for the APP, not for Oliva (see scripts/oliva/owned-paths.txt).
# Drop files named *.caddy here and restart the `gateway` service:
#
#     docker compose restart gateway
#
# Each file is imported into the gateway's single site block (http://:80).
# Caddy's `handle` directives are evaluated by matcher specificity, with the
# catch-all last; an app route will match before the default frontend proxy.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example 1 — proxy a new path to a sidecar service on app_network:
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# handle /metrics {
#     reverse_proxy metrics-exporter:9090
# }
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example 2 — serve a static response without touching the frontend:
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# handle /robots.txt {
#     respond "User-agent: *\nDisallow: /" 200
# }
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT here: the Content-Security-Policy. It lives in the gateway's main
# Caddyfile (owned by Oliva) and reads env vars so each environment can tweak
# it in one place. Define app-specific CSP overrides there, not here.
